# The sum of two intervals with one-limb bounds: the lower bounds added downward, the upper bounds
# upward; the empty set when an operand is empty (its lower bound is then +inf).
kernel:        interval_add_1
input:         stored xl
input:         stored xu
input:         stored yl
input:         stored yu
output:        zl
output:        zu
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the bounds are directed sums, and the empty set is selected after an explicit test

l  = add_down_1(xl, yl)
h  = add_up_1(xu, yu)
nx = lt(xl, const inf)
ny = lt(yl, const inf)
ne = and(nx, ny)
mi = neg(const inf)
zl = select(ne, l, const inf)
zu = select(ne, h, mi)
